WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Step number four, posting the MP3 audio file to the church website.

00:06.000 --> 00:15.000
If the form filled out for this sermon included a scripture reference, we will first get the scripture text so that it can be added to the website along with the audio file.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
In this video, we will use BibleGateway.com to get the scripture text.

00:20.000 --> 00:28.000
Enter the scripture reference and then select the English Standard Version, which is the version normally used at all saints.

00:30.000 --> 00:50.000
Then click the magnifying glass to retrieve the text.

00:50.000 --> 00:59.000
Clicking on the printer icon will display a simpler view of the text, which makes it easy to select and copy.

00:59.000 --> 01:05.000
Normally, we don't include the headings shown in the text and just select and copy the verses of scripture.

01:05.000 --> 01:18.000
Select the verses of scripture and then copy them to the clipboard.

01:18.000 --> 01:25.000
To save the scripture text for later, paste it into a text editor like notepad on Windows.

01:25.000 --> 01:32.000
To access the Squarespace website configuration pages, enter config after the church website address as shown.

01:32.000 --> 01:36.000
Then log in with your email address and password.

01:36.000 --> 01:47.000
After logging in under website, select the pages link.

01:47.000 --> 02:02.000
Then scroll down to find the listen section and select sermons.

02:02.000 --> 02:05.000
The sermon we're about to upload is from February.

02:05.000 --> 02:09.000
We try to keep sermons on the website for one year.

02:09.000 --> 02:17.000
When you are about to upload the first sermon of a month, scroll down to the bottom of the list to see if that month from the previous year should be removed.

02:17.000 --> 02:32.000
Use the scroll bar to scroll down to the end. You may have to do this two or three times to get to the very end.

02:32.000 --> 02:37.000
Here we see that there are still some sermons from January as well as February from the previous year.

02:37.000 --> 02:44.000
To remove these older sermons, start by clicking on the oldest one.

02:44.000 --> 02:52.000
Then to select additional sermons to remove, hold down the shift key and click on the others one at a time.

03:02.000 --> 03:15.000
Then click on the remove button near the bottom.

03:15.000 --> 03:19.000
Click confirm.

03:19.000 --> 03:35.000
You can check that the sermons have been removed by scrolling down to the bottom again.

03:35.000 --> 03:41.000
Return to the top of the list.

03:41.000 --> 03:47.000
Then click the plus sign to add a new sermon.

03:47.000 --> 04:05.000
For the title of the post, enter the sermon title from the online sermon form.

04:05.000 --> 04:11.000
When you hover over the body of the post, you will see plus signs that allow you to add content to the post.

04:11.000 --> 04:23.000
Click on the plus sign at the very top to add a new text object.

04:23.000 --> 04:37.000
In this new line of text, enter the date of the sermon.

04:37.000 --> 04:46.000
Then click the plus sign under the text and select audio.

04:46.000 --> 04:50.000
Sometimes clicking this icon to upload doesn't work well.

04:50.000 --> 05:06.000
We will instead drag and drop the MP3 file into this section of the page.

05:06.000 --> 05:09.000
The MP3 file will upload.

05:09.000 --> 05:22.000
When it is finished uploading, it should read the title and speaker data from the metadata you entered in the Audacity program.

05:22.000 --> 05:36.000
Next, to provide a download link, select the design tab at the top. Then select show download link and click apply.

05:36.000 --> 05:46.000
To add the scripture reference, click the plus sign immediately under the audio object.

05:46.000 --> 05:54.000
Select mock down.

05:54.000 --> 06:11.000
This will allow you to add formatted text, start by adding the scripture book and verse information.

06:11.000 --> 06:33.000
Then copy over the scripture verses.

06:33.000 --> 06:51.000
To add some formatting, first we will make the heading display in bold text after adding ESV after it to show that this is from the ESV translation.

06:51.000 --> 07:03.000
Then to make the verse numbers display as smaller text and shown slightly above the rest of the text or in superscript, we will add soup tags around each verse number as shown.

07:21.000 --> 07:41.000
Click apply to save the mark down object.

07:41.000 --> 07:47.000
Now click the options tab.

07:47.000 --> 08:06.000
We need to change the author value from our name to the speakers name. Click on the author field and select the speaker from the list if it exists. In this case, we will just select guest speaker.

08:06.000 --> 08:13.000
Now click save and publish to save this new post and make it available for people to see.

08:13.000 --> 08:26.000
When the post is saved, at first it will have today's date shown. We will need to change it to the actual date of the service. Click the edit button next to the sermon.

08:26.000 --> 08:43.000
Then click the date and time under published and change it to the date and time of the service.

08:43.000 --> 08:53.000
Click save to save the changes.

08:53.000 --> 09:06.000
The sermon posting should now be complete. You may want to test the recording by clicking the play button and then clicking forward to different sections.

09:06.000 --> 09:18.000
Good morning everyone. You may be seated. I am a little horse today. I knew I wasn't preaching this morning and so I yelled louder than I do.

09:18.000 --> 09:29.000
It's coming to pick up ball jars of clippings. We're always visiting people eaters. God governs his people with justice. He shows me. We are the laborers.

09:29.000 --> 09:50.000
The laborers have sent my prayer for you. You, oh God, are the living word presence. Encourage us to search for you and to let our searching help others find you through Jesus Christ our Lord. Amen.

